python3 translate.py "$(inputs.gff.path)" "$(inputs.genome.path)" "$(inputs.min_len)" translated_pseudogenes.fasta","inputs":[{"name":"gff","label":"GFF3 Annotation file","type":"data"},{"name":"genome","label":"Genome FASTA file","type":"data"},{"name":"min_len","label":"Minimum translated fragment length","type":"integer","value":50}],"outputs":[{"name":"fasta","label":"Six-frame translated pseudogenes","type":"data","format":"fasta","from_work_dir":"translated_pseudogenes.fasta"}],"help":{"format":"markdown","content":"### What it does
This tool recovers pseudogenized loci from genomic annotations and translates them for downstream HMM screening.

It parses `pseudogenic_transcript` features and child `exon` coordinates from a GFF3 file, extracts corresponding nucleotide sequence from the genome FASTA, stitches exons in coordinate order, reverse-complements minus-strand transcripts, and translates each stitched locus in all six reading frames. Translated sequences shorter than the requested minimum amino acid length are discarded.

### Inputs
- GFF3 annotation file containing `pseudogenic_transcript` and `exon` features.
- Genome FASTA with sequence IDs matching the GFF3 seqids.
